# Portfolio project rules

## Stack
React 19 + TypeScript, TanStack Router (file-based routes in `src/routes/`),
Tailwind v4 (tokens in `src/styles.css`), Vite. No other router, no CSS-in-JS.

## Read first
- `docs/PRD.md` — what we're building and why
- `docs/content-model.md` — JSON shapes, the source of truth for content
- `docs/design-system.md` — tokens, type scale, layout rhythm

## Hard rules
1. **No hardcoded colors.** Use semantic tokens (`bg-background`, `text-accent`).
   Never `text-white`, `bg-black`, `bg-[#...]`.
2. **Content lives in JSON.** Never hardcode copy, links, or case study text in a
   component. Add it to `src/content/*.json` and read it through `src/lib/content.ts`.
3. **Routes:** one file per page under `src/routes/`. The string in
   `createFileRoute("/path")` must match the filename (dots = slashes).
   Never edit `src/routeTree.gen.ts`.
4. **Every page defines `head()`** with a unique title, description, `og:title`,
   and `og:description`.
5. **Mobile-first.** Every new section must work at 360px wide.
6. **Links:** use `<Link to="/work/$slug" params={{ slug }}>`, never
   `<a href={\`/work/${slug}\`}>`.
7. Components stay small and presentational; put shared bits in `src/components/`.

## When adding a case study
Add one object to `src/content/case-studies.json` following the schema in
`docs/content-model.md`. Do not create a new route file — `/work/$slug` handles it.

## Definition of done
Typechecks, renders at 360/768/1280, no console errors, unique metadata,
no hardcoded color or copy.
